/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.prof*
.env*
.DS_Store
*.log
# The flake log is COMMITTED EVIDENCE (record-flakes.sh: "never edited by
# hand, never truncated") — the blanket *.log above silently defeated that
# contract for the whole pre-split regime; the observations it swallowed are
# preserved in benches/records/archive-2026-08-13/flakes.log.
!benches/flakes.log
# A history reset rotates the live flake log into a dated archive
# (benches/records/<date>/flakes.log); without its own negation the blanket
# *.log swallows the rotated copy — the 045 rotation exposed the gap.
!benches/records/*/flakes.log
.idea/
.vscode/
# rdlt runtime work directories (WAL etc.)
.rdlt/
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/
toolbox/
benches/results/raw/
benches/results/selftest-protocol.json
# Airbyte competitor: machine-local connection ids written by setup.py, and any
# optional local venv for the driver.
benches/competitors/airbyte/state.json
benches/competitors/airbyte/.venv/
benches/competitors/airbyte/__pycache__/

# Python proof connector: interpreter bytecode cache (the certify and
# stub-check venvs already live under target/, which is ignored wholesale).
connectors/python/rdlt-connector-pyjsonl/__pycache__/

# Internal development records — the working memory of the project's
# plan-driven process (feature specs, the session driver document, the
# speckit machinery). They live on disk for local work and stay out of
# the public repository.
/specs/
/CLAUDE.md
/REFACTORING.md
/.claude/
/.specify/
/docs/superpowers/
/2026-07-18-rdlt-engine-design.md
# Run artifacts at the repo root (workdirs from ad-hoc pipeline runs),
# and the on-disk TMPDIR the gate uses to stay off the RAM tmpfs.
/.rdlt*/
# Nested benchmark/example workdirs, including per-load spellings.
**/.rdlt*/
/.tmp-real/
# Scanner hook session state — local telemetry, never part of the tree.
/.mimosa/
# cargo's own state under a repo-local CARGO_HOME: caches and the registry
# symlink (a machine-local absolute path). Only mutants.toml is ours.
/.cargo/*
!/.cargo/mutants.toml
# External review reports delivered into the root; worked from, never
# shipped — a blanket `git add -A` must not sweep them in.
/SECURITY_CODE_REVIEW*.md
/CODEX_SECURITY_REVIEW*.md
